>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ica.2021.120668","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQM/tree/ece824419c9006fe66436daf233822b75533b82f/tmQM","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/1566024.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. Both carboxyl termini have dissociated as free CO₂ in the optimized coordinates. Each remaining pyridylselenium–CH₂ fragment is neutral with an odd electron count; Retain Se–C, Place one radical on each terminal CH₂. Two Cl⁻ balance Pd(II). The electrons can delocalize between Se and carbon. The local radical symbols do not determine total spin. Localized 12 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

>  <UPSTREAM_COMPARISON>
Not equivalent

>  <SPIN_REVIEW>
Spin coupling awaits verification

